{"id":"girvan-yuddha-bikram-shah","order":3075,"name":"Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah","region":"south-asia","region_label":"South Asia","realm":"King of Nepal","era":"early-modern","era_label":"Early Modern","blurb":null,"reign_from":1799,"reign_to":1816,"year_from":1799,"year_to":1816,"wp":"Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah","source":"wikidata","civ_wiki":null,"sources":{"wikidata":"ok","wikipedia":"ok"},"qid":"Q2714587","wikidata_url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2714587","wd_label":"Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah Deva","wd_description":"King of Nepal (1797–1816)","birth_year":1797,"death_year":1816,"reign_wikidata":[1799,1816],"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/King_Girvan_Yuddhavikram_Shah_%281797-1816%29_LACMA_M.76.129.jpg?width=640","family_qid":"Q3274200","predecessor_qid":"Q2714575","successor_qid":"Q788541","father_qid":"Q2714575","mother_qid":"Q21069459","children_qids":["Q788541"],"birthplace_qid":"Q3037","deathplace_qid":"Q3037","position_qids":["Q19700527"],"family":"Shah dynasty","predecessor":"Rana Bahadur Shah","successor":"Rajendra of Nepal","predecessor_id":"rana-bahadur-shah","successor_id":"rajendra-bikram-shah","father":"Rana Bahadur Shah","father_id":"rana-bahadur-shah","mother":"Kantiwati Devi","children":["Rajendra of Nepal"],"birthplace":"Kathmandu","birthplace_coord":[85.32,27.71],"deathplace":"Kathmandu","deathplace_coord":[85.32,27.71],"positions":["King of Nepal"],"extract":"Girvan Yuddha Bikram Shah (Nepali: श्री ५ महाराजाधिराज गीर्वाणयुद्ध विक्रम शाह देव; 19 October 1797 – 20 November 1816) was King of Nepal. Although he was not the legitimate heir to the throne his father, King Rana Bahadur Shah, made him the heir for being the son of his favourite wife Kantavati Jha.\nGirvan Yuddha ascended the throne at the age of 1 and 1/2 years when his father abdicated to become an ascetic. He ruled under the regency of Queen Tripurasundari of Nepal and Prime Minister Bhimsen Thapa. He died at age 19 and was succeeded by his young son Rajendra Bikram Shah.","wp_description":"King of Nepal from 1799 to 1816","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girvan_Yuddha_Bikram_Shah","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/King_Girvan_Yuddhavikram_Shah_%281797-1816%29_%28restoration%29.jpg","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/King_Girvan_Yuddhavikram_Shah_%281797-1816%29_%28restoration%29.jpg/960px-King_Girvan_Yuddhavikram_Shah_%281797-1816%29_%28restoration%29.jpg","chat_ready":false,"display_from":1799,"display_to":1816}